{"description":"Stand up the coordinator: a process that joins the tailnet as its own node, accepts WebSocket connections, authenticates each one by resolving the caller's tailnet identity from the connection's remote address, and persists to a pure-Go SQLite store.\n\nThis is the item that realises the largest scope reduction in the design — there is no credential handling, no session store and no user table to build, because authentication is a lookup.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. The coordinator joins the tailnet from inside its container with no host networking and no Tailscale sidecar.\n2. Every accepted connection resolves to an authenticated tailnet identity; a connection whose identity cannot be resolved is refused and the refusal is logged.\n3. The listener binds to the tailnet interface only. A connection attempt from a non-tailnet interface cannot reach it, and this is verified by test rather than by inspection.\n4. Persistence uses the pure-Go SQLite driver, so the coordinator binary has no CGO dependency.\n5. The schema is created and migrated on first start without manual steps.\n6. No password, token, session identifier or user record exists anywhere in the store."}